{"page":300,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.04911,"w":0.29692,"h":0.01851,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"286 Chapter 4: Applications of Derivatives"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.09056,"w":0.593,"h":0.02962,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"about why this is important in Chapter 5. Using this notation, we restate the solutions of Example 1, as follows:"},{"x":0.50702,"y":0.1313,"w":0.11175,"h":0.0217,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"2x dx = x2 + C,"},{"x":0.50702,"y":0.17862,"w":0.14661,"h":0.01723,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"cos x dx = sin x + C,"},{"x":0.52034,"y":0.18963,"w":0.22728,"h":0.07735,"fs":0.01353,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"x + 2e2xb dx = ln 0 x0 + e2x + C."},{"x":0.5109,"y":0.19456,"w":0.01714,"h":0.06906,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"a1"},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.25278,"w":0.59305,"h":0.06031,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"This notation is related to the main application of antiderivatives, which will be explored in Chapter 5. Antiderivatives play a key role in computing limits of certain infinite sums, an unexpected and wonderfully useful role that is described in a central result of Chapter 5, called the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.33501,"w":0.17855,"h":0.01687,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Example 6 Evaluate"},{"x":0.56666,"y":0.36258,"w":0.11992,"h":0.0217,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"(x2 - 2x + 5) dx."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.37321,"w":0.59302,"h":0.06906,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"Solution If we recognize that (x3>3) - x2 + 5x is an antiderivative of x2 - 2x + 5, we can evaluate the integral as"},{"x":0.62924,"y":0.43991,"w":0.09465,"h":0.02281,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"antiderivative $++%++&"},{"x":0.49155,"y":0.46159,"w":0.15345,"h":0.0246,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"(x2 - 2x + 5) dx = x3"},{"x":0.63431,"y":0.46449,"w":0.16687,"h":0.03575,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"3 - x2 + 5x + C. \" arbitrary constant"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.50807,"w":0.59308,"h":0.02962,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"If we do not recognize the antiderivative right away, we can generate it term-by-term with the Sum, Difference, and Constant Multiple Rules:"},{"x":0.65815,"y":0.54429,"w":0.07519,"h":0.0354,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"2x dx + L"},{"x":0.42566,"y":0.5488,"w":0.13285,"h":0.0217,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"(x2 - 2x + 5) dx ="},{"x":0.58349,"y":0.55311,"w":0.04968,"h":0.0174,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"x2 dx -"},{"x":0.73503,"y":0.55391,"w":0.02768,"h":0.01427,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"5 dx"},{"x":0.58349,"y":0.59659,"w":0.0652,"h":0.0174,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"x2 dx - 2"},{"x":0.66632,"y":0.59676,"w":0.05925,"h":0.01723,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"x dx + 5"},{"x":0.74319,"y":0.59739,"w":0.02768,"h":0.01427,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"1 dx"},{"x":0.54147,"y":0.61335,"w":0.04815,"h":0.06906,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= ax3"},{"x":0.57894,"y":0.61335,"w":0.25996,"h":0.06906,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"3 + C1b - 2ax2 2 + C2b + 5(x + C3)"},{"x":0.54147,"y":0.67508,"w":0.03764,"h":0.0246,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= x3"},{"x":0.56842,"y":0.67797,"w":0.22961,"h":0.02883,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"3 + C1 - x2 - 2C2 + 5x + 5C3."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.71314,"w":0.59302,"h":0.03513,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"This formula is more complicated than it needs to be. If we combine C1, -2C2, and 5C3 into a single arbitrary constant C = C1 - 2C2 + 5C3, the formula simplifies to"},{"x":0.55494,"y":0.75161,"w":0.01319,"h":0.01505,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"x3"},{"x":0.55744,"y":0.75451,"w":0.12332,"h":0.02883,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"3 - x2 + 5x + C"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.78882,"w":0.59302,"h":0.02962,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"and still gives all the possible antiderivatives there are. For this reason, we recommend that you go right to the final form even if you elect to integrate term-by-term. Write"},{"x":0.69101,"y":0.82505,"w":0.07519,"h":0.0354,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"2x dx + L"},{"x":0.45852,"y":0.82956,"w":0.13285,"h":0.0217,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"(x2 - 2x + 5) dx ="},{"x":0.61634,"y":0.83386,"w":0.04968,"h":0.0174,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"x2 dx -"},{"x":0.76788,"y":0.83466,"w":0.02768,"h":0.01427,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"5 dx"},{"x":0.57434,"y":0.86567,"w":0.03763,"h":0.0246,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= x3"},{"x":0.60128,"y":0.86857,"w":0.12739,"h":0.02883,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"3 - x2 + 5x + C."},{"x":0.32334,"y":0.90436,"w":0.593,"h":0.02962,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Find the simplest antiderivative you can for each part and add the arbitrary constant of integration at the end.\b"}]}